"proof_obligation": "preservation",
"diagnosis": "The loop invariant requires (pos == i - 1 || arr[pos + 1] > elem). Once pos is set to some index and a later element differs from elem and is smaller than elem (e.g. arr[1142]=1796=elem, arr[1143]=1795), pos stays put, pos != i - 1, and arr[pos+1] < elem. The array is not required to be sorted, so the body cannot maintain this conjunct. It is also unnecessary: the postcondition's disjunct pos <= arr.Length - 1 follows from 0 <= pos < i <= arr.Length. Fix: weaken the invariant to pos == -1 || (0 <= pos < i && arr[pos] == elem)."}

